From a5483a49e98c6d16b6f71093ab3d70e8e63f6e3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 04:47:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: capture MT6897 DIS state at C-PHY power phases

Add a read-only MMSYS helper returning the DIS routing registers, the configuration gate bank 2 status word and the DIS merge-interrupt register. The caller must already hold the parent runtime-PM and configuration-clock references, matching the routing restore contract.

Use it from the MT6897 C-PHY link path to log bounded, once-per-power-on evidence before the 26M gate is enabled, after routing restore, at the first host command and at the first IRQ timeout before the existing enable/reset recovery. Also capture DSI INTEN/INTSTA/CON/MODE at the latter two points. The reads change no register or clock state.

Portable tests cover the bounded capture, the 26M failure unwind and both banks' read-only state, and check the required phase ordering.

These readbacks are trial evidence for the remaining physical resume failure; they do not assume that the 26M gate or interrupt routing is the cause.

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
